Z||000003||Oreif||04-24-2001||06:55 PM||||Cold @ idle mine is about 40 PSI<BR>Cold @ 2000 RPM is 60-70 PSI<BR>Hot @ idle about 25 PSI<BR>Hot 2000 RPM about 45-50 PSI<P>I use 10W-40 castrol GTX<BR>86 SE V-6 stock motor.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||04-24-2001||07:05 PM||||In the range of 35 - 60<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000005||ironhedno3||04-24-2001||07:40 PM||||good rule of thumb is 10psi for every 1000 rpms..stick with 5w30..heavier oils are just robbing you of slight horsepower..not to mention the tolerances from the factory are ste up for 5w30..ive seen some case which are few of heavy weight oils burning up wristpins||||reg||6
